  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, broad four-beat waddle with whole alternating steps and outward webbed palms. Quick travel becomes a brisk low scuttle, with a quiet back and a coherent paddle tail following the hips.",
    "attack": "A brief backward brace leads to a low bill-first shove and compact forward forefoot step, followed by a planted recovery. The bill, eyes and face remain one coherent skull mass.",
